# public/assets is TRACKED in this fork (2026-08-22). Upstream ignores it for
# size, but this fork already carries the ~1GB "DynastyOS Assets" library, and
# leaving public/assets out silently broke every fresh clone: conference
# logos, rivalry trophies, and location art are served from `assets/...`
# (webpack copies public/assets -> assets), so a clone without it renders
# broken-image icons across Standings/Scores. Whoever has the populated
# folder commits it once and every machine pulls working art.
# (If any single file exceeds GitHub's 100MB hard limit the push will name
# it — deal with that file individually rather than re-ignoring the folder.)

# Local archives / reference material, not source
.backup/
References/
Dynasty Save Test/

# Scratch. `output/` in particular is NOT app output — it's a drop folder that
# has collected unrelated documents, and a blanket `git add -A` committed a
# client invoice out of it once. Ignored so that cannot happen again.
output/
tmp/

# Machine-local Claude Code settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated user manual (regenerate with `npm run manual` from docs/manual/)
# Globbed rather than named: the file is titled after the app, which the
# DynastyOS rename changed once already.
docs/manual/*.pdf
docs/manual/manual.rendered.html

# Throwaway HTML used to eyeball a component in a browser mid-build.
.*-preview.html
